 "notes": "Solid magenta contour of Fig. 4 (file boundsSK_g_vs_ma_8.pdf in the e-print): 95% C.L. observed exclusion from Super-Kamiokande data (four SK phases combined) on the diffuse galactic-SN ALP flux via a p -> p gamma. The paper's Lagrangian L = g_a d_mu a/(2 m_N) C_ap pbar gamma^mu gamma_5 p with g_ap = g_a C_ap is already the canonical normalisation (g_ap = C_p m_N/f_a), so no 2m_N conversion applied; the figure y-axis is g_ap directly. Model choice: C_ap = -0.47, C_an = 0 (KSVZ-inspired), i.e. g_an = 0; plotted values are |g_ap|. The excluded region is a closed island (roughly 1-64 MeV, g_ap ~2.5e-5 to ~2.3e-4), emitted as the closed boundary in the figure's native traversal order (lower edge -> right tip -> upper edge -> left edge at 1 MeV). The dashed contour (lower reach ~1e-5, Hyper-Kamiokande) is a projection and was excluded. Axis calibration from frame corners and decade/minor tick marks, cross-checked against the abstract's quoted range 2e-5 - 2e-4 for 1-70 MeV and the HK ~1e-5 reach. Masses converted MeV -> eV (x1e6).",
